{"schemaVersion":1,"nct":"NCT07440225","source":"https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT07440225","apiSource":"https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT07440225","attribution":"Courtesy of the National Library of Medicine","fetchedAt":"2026-10-07T16:55:44.977Z","studySha256":"d78557cbaab5b22aaaae5f72fe999865c81b13f0c6c88c13351b96d4a7739a6e","study":{"protocolSection":{"identificationModule":{"nctId":"NCT07440225","briefTitle":"A Clinical Trial of EYE201/MK-8748 in People With Macular Degeneration (MK-8748-002)","officialTitle":"A Randomized Double-masked, Multicenter, 3-arm, Pivotal Phase 2/3 Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of Intravitreal (IVT) EYE201/MK-8748 Compared to Aflibercept (2 mg) in Participants With Neovascular Age-related Macular Degeneration (NVAMD)","acronym":"MALBEC"},"statusModule":{"statusVerifiedDate":"2026-09","overallStatus":"RECRUITING","expandedAccessInfo":{"hasExpandedAccess":false},"startDateStruct":{"date":"2026-03-27","type":"ACTUAL"},"primaryCompletionDateStruct":{"date":"2028-06-30","type":"ESTIMATED"},"completionDateStruct":{"date":"2028-06-30","type":"ESTIMATED"},"studyFirstSubmitDate":"2026-02-23","studyFirstSubmitQcDate":"2026-02-23","studyFirstPostDateStruct":{"date":"2026-02-27","type":"ACTUAL"},"lastUpdateSubmitDate":"2026-09-30","lastUpdatePostDateStruct":{"date":"2026-10-02","type":"ACTUAL"}},"sponsorCollaboratorsModule":{"leadSponsor":{"name":"EyeBiotech Ltd.","class":"INDUSTRY"}},"descriptionModule":{"briefSummary":"Researchers are looking for new ways to treat neovascular age-related macular degeneration (NVAMD).\n\nAvailable standard (usual) treatments for NVAMD, such as aflibercept, may not work for every person. Researchers want to learn if a trial medicine called tiespectus (also called MK-8748 or EYE201) can treat NVAMD.\n\nThe goal of this trial is to learn if tiespectus works as well as aflibercept to treat NVAMD."},"conditionsModule":{"conditions":["Macular Degeneration","Age-Related Macular Degeneration","Choroidal Neovascularization","Wet Macular Degeneration"]},"designModule":{"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","phases":["PHASE2","PHASE3"],"designInfo":{"allocation":"RANDOMIZED","interventionModel":"PARALLEL","primaryPurpose":"TREATMENT","maskingInfo":{"masking":"TRIPLE","whoMasked":["PARTICIPANT","CARE_PROVIDER","INVESTIGATOR"]}},"enrollmentInfo":{"count":960,"type":"ESTIMATED"}},"armsInterventionsModule":{"armGroups":[{"label":"Tiespectus Low Dose","type":"EXPERIMENTAL","description":"Participants receive 3 initial administrations of tiespectus low dose every 4 weeks (Q4W), then continue to receive tiespectus low dose every 8 weeks (Q8W) until week 48. After week 48, participants will be treated at intervals determined based on individualized response to treatment, up to week 92.","interventionNames":["Drug: Tiespectus"]},{"label":"Tiespectus High Dose","type":"EXPERIMENTAL","description":"Participants receive 3 initial administrations of tiespectus high dose Q4W, then continue to receive tiespectus high dose Q8W until week 48. After week 48, participants will be treated at intervals determined based on individualized response to treatment, up to week 92","interventionNames":["Drug: Tiespectus"]},{"label":"Aflibercept 2 mg","type":"ACTIVE_COMPARATOR","description":"Participants receive 3 initial administrations of aflibercept, then continue to receive aflibercept Q8W until week 92","interventionNames":["Drug: Aflibercept"]}],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"Tiespectus","description":"Administered by intravitreal (IVT) injection","armGroupLabels":["Tiespectus High Dose","Tiespectus Low Dose"],"otherNames":["EYE201","MK-8748"]},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Aflibercept","description":"Administered by intravitreal injection (IVT)","armGroupLabels":["Aflibercept 2 mg"],"otherNames":["Eylea®"]}]},"outcomesModule":{"primaryOutcomes":[{"measure":"Mean Change in Best-Corrected Visual Acuity (BCVA) [Early Treatment of Diabetic Retinopathy Study (ETDRS Letters)] From Baseline to Year 1","description":"Participants' BCVA in the study eye will be measured using the Early Treatment of Diabetic Retinopathy (ETDRS) methodology. The ETDRS letter score ranges from 0 to 100, with a higher score indicating better visual acuity. Mean change in ETDRS letters from baseline to Year 1 will be assessed.","timeFrame":"Baseline and Year 1"}],"secondaryOutcomes":[{"measure":"Mean Change in BCVA (ETDRS Letters) From Baseline (Day 1) Over Time to Year 1","description":"Participants' BCVA in the study eye will be measured using the Early Treatment of Diabetic Retinopathy (ETDRS) methodology. The ETDRS letter score ranges from 0 to 100, with a higher score indicating better visual acuity. The mean change in BCVA from baseline over time to year 1 will be assessed.","timeFrame":"Up to Year 1"},{"measure":"Proportion of Participants Who Gain ≥5 ETDRS Letters at Year 1","description":"Participants' BCVA in the study eye will be measured using the Early Treatment of Diabetic Retinopathy (ETDRS) methodology. The ETDRS letter score ranges from 0 to 100, with a higher score indicating better visual acuity.","timeFrame":"Year 1"},{"measure":"Proportion of Participants Who Gain ≥10 ETDRS Letters at Year 1","description":"Participants' BCVA in the study eye will be measured using the Early Treatment of Diabetic Retinopathy (ETDRS) methodology. The ETDRS letter score ranges from 0 to 100, with a higher score indicating better visual acuity.","timeFrame":"Year 1"},{"measure":"Proportion of Participants Who Gain ≥15 ETDRS Letters at Year 1","description":"Participants' BCVA in the study eye will be measured using the Early Treatment of Diabetic Retinopathy (ETDRS) methodology. The ETDRS letter score ranges from 0 to 100, with a higher score indicating better visual acuity.","timeFrame":"Year 1"},{"measure":"Proportion of Participants Who Lose ≥5 ETDRS Letters at Year 1","description":"Participants' BCVA in the study eye will be measured using the Early Treatment of Diabetic Retinopathy (ETDRS) methodology. The ETDRS letter score ranges from 0 to 100, with a higher score indicating better visual acuity.","timeFrame":"Year 1"},{"measure":"Proportion of Participants Who Lose ≥10 ETDRS Letters at Year 1","description":"Participants' BCVA in the study eye will be measured using the Early Treatment of Diabetic Retinopathy (ETDRS) methodology. The ETDRS letter score ranges from 0 to 100, with a higher score indicating better visual acuity.","timeFrame":"Year 1"},{"measure":"Proportion of Participants Who Lose ≥15 ETDRS Letters at Year 1","description":"Participants' BCVA in the study eye will be measured using the Early Treatment of Diabetic Retinopathy (ETDRS) methodology. The ETDRS letter score ranges from 0 to 100, with a higher score indicating better visual acuity.","timeFrame":"Year 1"},{"measure":"Mean Change in Spectral Domain Optical Coherence Tomography (SD-OCT) Central Subfield Thickness (CST) From Baseline (Day 1) To Year 1","description":"CST will be measured in microns using SD-OCT. Mean change in CST from baseline to Year 1 will be assessed.","timeFrame":"Baseline and Year 1"},{"measure":"Number of Participants who Experience One or More Systemic Adverse Events (AEs)","description":"An AE is any untoward medical occurrence associated with the use of a drug in humans, whether or not considered drug-related. Therefore, an AE can be any unfavorable and unintended sign (including an abnormal clinical laboratory finding, for example), symptom, or disease temporally associated with the use of a medicinal product, whether or not considered related to the medicinal product.","timeFrame":"Up to approximately 96 weeks"},{"measure":"Number of Participants who Experience One or More Ocular AEs","description":"An ocular adverse event (OAE) is defined as any untoward medical occurrence involving the eye or ocular adnexa (including eyelids, conjunctiva, lacrimal apparatus, extraocular muscles, and orbit) that:\n\nOccurs or worsens after the first administration of the investigational product (IP) or a study-related ocular procedure, and does not necessarily have a causal relationship with the IP or procedure.\n\nOAEs include, but are not limited to, changes in: Symptoms (e.g., ocular pain, photophobia, floaters, blurred vision), Visual function (e.g., best-corrected visual acuity \\[BCVA\\], visual field). Intraocular pressure (IOP), Anterior segment findings (e.g., conjunctival hyperemia, keratitis, anterior chamber inflammation), Posterior segment findings (e.g., vitreous inflammation, retinal hemorrhages, retinal tears or detachment, macular edema), or ocular adnexa (e.g., eyelid edema, ptosis)","timeFrame":"Up to approximately 96 weeks"}]},"eligibilityModule":{"eligibilityCriteria":"The main inclusion criteria include but are not limited to the following:\n\n* Has treatment naive choroidal neovascularization (CNV) secondary to age-related macular degeneration (AMD) including subfoveal, juxtafoveal and extrafoveal lesions or retinal angiomatous proliferations (RAP) and polypoidal choroidal vascularization (PCV) lesions in at least one eye (study eye)\n* The diagnosis of neovascular age-related macular degeneration (NVAMD) must have been made within 21 days prior to starting study treatment\n\nThe main exclusion criteria include but are not limited to the following\n\n* Has uncontrolled blood pressure at screening\n* History of any prior macular laser photocoagulation in the study eye\n* History of uveitis in either eye\n* History of cataract surgery, minimally invasive glaucoma surgery, or Yttrium-Aluminium Garnet (Yag) laser capsulotomy in the study eye within 90 days before entering the study\n* Has uncontrolled glaucoma in the study eye\n* Active retinal disease other than the condition under investigation in the study eye\n* Has previously received anti- vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF) therapy or other intravitreal (IVT) therapy in the study eye","healthyVolunteers":false,"sex":"ALL","m